# hypernix.deep_fryer

2-tier model-weight perturbation: LightFry (regulariser) / HeavyFry (severe). Reversible via snapshot.

## Documentation pages

- [DeepFryer](../../#/docs/DeepFryer) · [MDXL source](pages/DeepFryer.mdxl)

## API reference

[Open the API reference source](pages/api-reference.mdxl)

### `Fryer()`

Base deep-fryer. Subclasses set noise intensity + sparsity.

### `Fryer.save_pristine() -> int`

Store the untouched state dict so :meth:`un_fry` can restore

### `Fryer.un_fry() -> int`

Restore the last pristine snapshot. Returns the number of

### `Fryer.fry() -> dict[str, int]`

Perturb a ``fraction`` of each matching parameter's elements

### `LightFry()`

Mild regularising perturbation. Defaults: 2% of elements,

### `HeavyFry()`

Severe perturbation. Defaults: 30% of elements, 0.5× param-std

### `deep_fryer(tier, model, fraction=None, noise_std=None, patterns=(), seed=0, **extra) -> Fryer`

Construct a deep-fryer tier by short name.

